market_sections={
'fashion-line-business-plan': h('Positioning, acquisition and production checks')+table('Fictional launch decisions to validate',['Decision','Initial plan','Evidence before scaling'],[['Customer and occasion','Mix-and-match workwear for a narrow local buyer group','Five buyer conversations and fit feedback; record objections'],['Competitive alternatives','Existing wardrobe, secondhand and comparable local labels','Compare fit, total delivered price and availability; do not claim uniqueness without evidence'],['Acquisition','A fitting event and a small product-content test within the $300 ad allowance','Track paid retained orders, not only likes or signups'],['Production gate','Approve a size sample before the 140-unit commitment','Document measurements, defects, delivery and rework responsibility'],['Operations owner','Owner handles fit questions, packing and returns','Time a pilot order and inspect returned condition']])+p('Keep a release calendar with sample approval, production confirmation, photography, stock receipt, launch and first review. Do not announce a delivery date before the supplier schedule and packing capacity support it. If fit feedback requires a pattern change, revise the quote and cash dates before committing the remaining production payment. A new style is a separate inventory decision, not an automatic reward for a busy launch.'),
'ecommerce-business-plan':h('Market evidence, acquisition and fulfillment controls')+table('Fictional store planning decisions',['Area','Initial choice','Evidence to keep'],[['Customer problem','One defined product use case','Buyer interviews and reasons people decline'],['Alternatives','Comparable product, delivered price and delivery promise','Dated comparison; no invented competitor defects'],['Acquisition test','$900 maximum across explicitly named channels','Deduplicated orders and actual spend, not platform totals added together'],['Fulfillment','Ship from the 300-unit opening purchase','Stock receipt checks, dispatch times and exception log'],['Customer support','Owner answers pre-sale and return questions','Support time and recurring confusion by product']])+p('Write the promised dispatch window only after checking receiving, packing and carrier handoff. If a supplier delay means orders cannot be fulfilled as promised, revise the public promise and customer handling process rather than treating an order as complete when a label is created. Test one variable at a time where practical: changing price, channel, audience and shipping promise simultaneously makes it hard to explain a result. The plan should name who can stop spending when the cash or fulfillment assumption fails.'),
'recruitment-company-business-plan':h('Validate demand and define a controlled delivery process')+table('Fictional agency go-to-market plan',['Area','Initial plan','Verification'],[['Buyer','Small employers hiring operations roles','Confirm live requirements, decision maker and fee authority'],['Differentiation','A focused briefing and documented candidate assessment','Compare the actual buyer alternatives; avoid unsupported success-rate claims'],['Acquisition','Founder-led conversations and permission-based referrals','Log qualified requirements and signed terms, not raw contact counts'],['Delivery','Brief, source, screen, present, coordinate and follow up','Acceptance criteria and client feedback at each stage'],['Candidate handling','Share only necessary agreed information','Record permissions and use controlled access, not a public dashboard']])+p('The first sales objective is to validate that employers will agree the service scope and fee event. It is not to send the largest number of resumes. Before a search starts, record role requirements, compensation information supplied by the client, interview responsibility, feedback timing and the point at which a fee can be invoiced. If the buyer cannot agree the brief or terms, do not count the request among the five accepted searches. Separate buyer-development time from delivery capacity so a growing pipeline does not create invisible overbooking.')
}
for item in articles:
 if item['slug'] in market_sections:
  item['body']=item['body'].replace('<h2>Sources and method</h2>',market_sections[item['slug']]+'<h2>Sources and method</h2>')

